    "command": "python3 /tmp/s4-hybriddna-fixtures.py",
    "date": "2026-10-16",
    "nfc_note": "llama.cpp's pinned revision has no input normalizer (no NFC code in src/), while minfer follows the `pre` rule's declared NFC; the plain-text corpus is therefore gated in its NFC-stable spelling here. The decomposed `café` entry is the one input where the two differ, and it stays gated for the qwen family where the definition is HuggingFace's tokenizer (ADR-0044).",
    "extra_note": "the last 8 entries are DNA-specific: the shared corpus would never exercise the <dna> rule, so a tag block, a lower-case block, a tail shorter than 6, a non-ACGT base, a block with no closing tag, text outside the tags and an all-N block are gated too"
  },
